==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Asilan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Assassinlan Pasalan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other Cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this Cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Like most other Nekoluga family members, this cat is meant to be used as a support unit. It is pointless to use it by itself; it has somewhat weak attack power and slow attack speed. With some powerful friends backing it up, though, it quickly shows its true value.

Asilan Pasalan is best used on a stage with plentiful fast enemies, such as [[Bore]] or [[Shy Boy]]. While slowed, the enemies will be unable to get into attacking range, and you can cut them down at your leisure. Its [[Cat Combo]] ([[Long-Legged (Combo)|Long-Legged]]) is also extremely useful, as when combined with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], they can slow enemies for '''more than 70% of the time''', which is almost at the same level as [[Miko Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Mitama the Oracle]], except from a far larger distance away. Notably, it also is able to target Metal enemies unlike many other generalist debuffers, which helps a lot in metal-heavy stages.

==='''True Form'''===
Assassinlan Pasalan's improved range makes it act like a less stackable version of Cyberpunk Cat. It has long range and similar damage, but lacks a blind spot.

==='''Talents'''===
Cost Down is merely a convenience, as this unit has very poor stackability. Due to the small improvement, it's not recommended. Slow and Survive are what can make this unit better, further increasing the similarity with Cyberpunk, who also has these Talents. Survive comes into play when this unit is attacked, allowing for a second chance in the battle, while Slow is a simple, direct improvement.

While Dodge and Health up can allow Assassinlan Pasalan to possibly tank some [[Wave Attack]]s or peons that reach him, both abilities do not work well with the unit's low health and long recharge.

